    "body": "Problem: Installing plugins during lockfile synchronization always writes the lockfile, even though its content is used during install. This might be a problem if the lockfile (itself or its parent directory) is not writeable (can only be read).\r\n\r\nSolution: Do not write the lockfile when installing directly from it. This is okay since the `src` and `rev` are used directly from the lockfile and don't change at this step. While potential change in `version` (that must be written to the lockfile) is handled in other code path.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFix #41017.",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-28T13:46:14Z",
